    "notes": "The payload family exercises the agent's ability to distinguish CPU-bound serialisation from everything else. The distinguishing evidence: threads busy (serialisation holds them), pool quiet (no DB), GC possibly elevated (string allocation), and /api/payload in the endpoint breakdown as the slow one. Without a serialisation-time metric in the snapshot, the agent must reason from absence (no pool pressure, no GC explosion, slow CPU-heavy endpoint) rather than from a direct signal. That is legitimate diagnosis, and the correct abstention afterwards shows the agent knows the boundary.\n"
